{"id":"86491800-e05a-4fe1-a96d-909d67b1eaf2","object":"chat.completion","created":1793870657,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Now applying the environ.py edit: a bounded int-or-none factory plus the new logging config entry.\n\n```python\nenviron_hash = \"fe2c531989c419f0b51b169a07f5ed826dcec7f95c0c5bc3a351805923c4f218\"\nr = replace_text_batch(\"deepinfer/environ.py\", [\n {\"old_text\": '''def _str(v: str | None, default: str = \"\") -> str:\n    return v if v is not None else default\n''',\n  \"new_text\": '''def _str(v: str | None, default: str = \"\") -> str:\n    return v if v is not None else default\n\n\ndef _int_or_none_at_least(v: str | None, minimum: int) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"未设置时返回 None（不限），否则解析为 >= minimum 的整数。\"\"\"\n    if v is None:\n        return None\n    parsed = int(v)\n    if parsed < minimum:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{parsed} must be >= {minimum}\")\n    return parsed\n'''},\n {\"old_text\": '''    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n''',\n  \"new_text\": '''    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none_at_least(*, minimum: int) -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: _int_or_none_at_least(v, minimum))\n'''},\n {\"old_text\": '''    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n''',\n  \"new_text\": '''    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.int_or_none_at_least(minimum=32)\n    \"普通诊断日志单个消息正文的最大字符数；未设置表示不限长。统计日志始终输出完整消息。\"\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n'''},\n], environ_hash)\nprint(r)\n```","reasoning_content":"I need to make edits. Let me plan environ.py edit: add a factory method `int_or_none_min` or similar and config entry. Requirements: attribute returns None when unset, else int >= 32; invalid raises ValueError with variable name. Descriptor wrapper prefixes name so fine.\n\nI'll add a helper function `_int_or_none_at_least(v, minimum)` and factory method `EnvVar.int_or_none_at_least(minimum=32)`. Then add config `DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.int_or_none_at_least(32)` in Logging section.\n\nNote empty string: int('') raises ValueError, wrapped with name. Good.\n\nLet me apply edits to environ.py using replace_text_batch with file_hash fe2c...\n\nEdits:\n1. After `_str` function add helper.\n2. After `int_or_none` staticmethod add factory.\n3. In Logging section add config line.\n\nLet me do it.\n\nThen logger.py: add max_message_chars param keyword-only? \"保留原有四个位置参数，新参数 max_message_chars 只能按名称传入\" — after use_color: bool = False add `*, max_message_chars: int | None = None`. Validate: if not None: isinstance(True)? bool not int: `isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int) or max_message_chars < 32` -> ValueError.\n\nAlso validate positional args? Not needed.\n\nIn format: first call super().format(record) gives msg with replacement done and record.message set. But we need message truncation applied after %s substitution, and not modify record.msg/args. Approach: build message ourselves? super().format(record) sets record.message = record.getMessage() (mutating record but that's standard; still doesn't modify msg/args). Then truncate: we need to truncate only the message body within msg, before prefixing. Simpler: compute formatted msg via super().format then do truncation on record.message portion? But exception text and stack_info appended. Better to do truncation before super().format by temporarily... no, can't modify record.\n\nAlternative: implement format like standard Formatter.format but we call super().format(record) which yields full text. We need to replace message body. record.message after super().format equals getMessage() (unless stack/exception... getMessage is full). So compute truncated = _truncate(record.message) and replace first occurrence of record.message in msg.\n\nCareful: format prefix contains record.message via `%` formatting; the message may appear in filename? unlikely. Use `msg.find(record.message)` like existing code. Then replace that occurrence: msg = msg[:i] + truncated + msg[i+len(record.message):]. But if keep_full_message is True, skip.\n\nBut requirement 2: budget only limits message body, not prefix/exception/stack_info. Using record.message replacement achieves this.\n\nAlso note super().format mutates record.message — acceptable.\n\nBut wait: if exception, record.message doesn't include traceback, good.\n\nOrder: color and newline handling after.\n\nTruncate function:\n```\n_MESSAGE_OMIT_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\ndef _truncate_message(msg, max_chars):\n    if max_chars is None or len(msg) <= max_chars:\n        return msg\n    marker = _MESSAGE_OMIT_MARKER\n    remaining = max_chars - len(marker)\n    if remaining <= 0:\n        return msg[:max_chars]  # hmm\n    head = (remaining + 1) // 2\n    tail = remaining - head\n    return msg[:head] + marker + (msg[-tail:] if tail else \"\")\n```\nCheck example: budget 32, marker len? \"...<omitted>...\" = 3+9+3 = 15. remaining=17, head=9, tail=8. ✓.\n\nremaining always >= 32-15=17 since max>=32, so fine but keep guard.\n\nkeep_full_message check: `if getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True`.\n\nDefault init: `max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS`. Import envs. logger.py importing environ — check circular? environ doesn't import logger. fine.\n\nAlso default init `_setup_logger` sets formatter each call, so re-init picks cached config. Good.\n\nstats_logger: `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nLet me check logger.py imports: need to import envs from deepinfer.environ. Do it.\n\nAlso careful: the format method's fast path uses record.message; after truncation record.message stays full-length original; msg contains truncated. `if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message` prefix = msg[:msg.find(record.message)] — if truncated message not present... find returns -1 -> prefix = msg[:-1] wrong. Better compute prefix before truncation? Let's restructure:\n\n```\ndef format(self, record):\n    message = record.getMessage()\n    msg = super().format(record)\n    if '\\n' in msg and record.message:\n        prefix = msg[:msg.find(record.message)]\n        msg = msg.replace('\\n', '\\n'+prefix)\n    truncated = self._truncate(message)\n    if truncated != message:\n        idx = msg.find(message)  # multi-line replaced message\n        ...\n```\nHmm multiline replacement puts prefix after newlines, message may be broken. Better: truncate before? We cannot pass to super. But we can do truncation by temporarily patching? Alternative: don't call super().format; reimplement format using record.message? Formatter.format uses record.message = record.getMessage(); then s = self.formatMessage(record); if record.exc_info... So we could set record.message? mutating record.message is fine (standard). We can compute:\n\n```\nmessage = record.getMessage()\ntruncated = self._truncate(message)\nrecord.message = truncated  # hmm, but standard sets it to full\nmsg = super().format(record)\n```\nBut super().format calls getMessage() again and overwrites record.message with full — actually Formatter.format: `record.message = record.getMessage()` then `s = self.formatMessage(record)`. So can't pre-set.\n\nCleanest: after super().format, compute msg, then replace using record.message (full, as set by super) once. Do the newline-multiline handling AFTER truncation, using truncated message for prefix detection. Let's do:\n\n```\ndef format(self, record):\n    msg = super().format(record)\n    message = record.message\n    if message and getattr(record,'keep_full_message',None) is not True:\n        truncated = self._truncate(message)\n        if truncated != message:\n            idx = msg.find(message)\n            if idx >= 0:\n                msg = msg[:idx] + truncated + msg[idx+len(message):]\n    # multiline prefix\n    if '\\n' in msg:\n        prefix = msg[: msg.find(truncated_or message...)]\n```\nHmm multiline prefix: original code uses record.message. If truncated, we should use truncated; but truncated may contain the marker. Simpler: compute prefix as everything before the message text in msg. Since we may have replaced, find the message we finally used.\n\nLet me define `final_message` variable = truncated or message. Then:\n```\nif '\\n' in msg and final_message:\n    idx = msg.find(final_message)\n    if idx >= 0:\n        prefix = msg[:idx]\n        msg = msg.replace('\\n', '\\n'+prefix)\n```\nWait but replacing newlines inside truncated message adds prefix — original behavior adds prefix to all newlines including message's internal ones. Fine.\n\nFor exception traceback, msg contains message then \"\\n\" traceback; prefix added to those too — same as original.\n\nEdge: if keep_full_message True, msg remains original behavior: prefix = msg[:msg.find(record.message)]. Using final_message=message gives same.\n\nCareful: original code `if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message` where record.message could be \"\" -> skip. With final_message same.\n\nAlso if truncation removed newlines? Truncated message may not include newline but msg contains ones from traceback etc.\n\nOK.\n\nNow note: record.message may be empty string while msg has content. fine.\n\nLet me write edits.\n\nAlso need to double-check base formatter init signature \"保留原有四个位置参数\" — the four are fmt, datefmt, high_precision, use_color. Keep as positional-or-keyword.\n\nNow write."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10064,"completion_tokens":2346,"total_tokens":12410,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":3968},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1836},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":3968,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":6096},"system_finge